From c3ad0c0e28ddc3364b66e7075370e4f7d67c6eee Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
Date: Thu, 17 Sep 2026 08:20:54 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] tools/structure: catch TypeError too in applyCallableIndex's
 variadic retry

applyCallableIndex (added in 3.8.1 for callable powerIndex entries like
`s[ca.vertcat, ['x','y']]`) tries `p(r)` first and falls back to `p(*r)`
only on NotImplementedError, on the assumption that a variadic free
function like vertcat raises NotImplementedError when handed a single
list argument it can't match.

It doesn't: vertcat/horzcat/veccat are SWIG-overloaded functions, so
`_vertcat((r,))` (a one-tuple holding the list) fails C++ overload
resolution and raises TypeError instead - "Wrong number or type of
arguments for overloaded function '_vertcat'". The except clause never
catches it, so the p(*r) retry this function exists for never runs, and
every callable-powerIndex lookup using vertcat/horzcat fails outright.

Reproduces on any platform running the test suite (not riscv64-specific):
tools.Toolstests.test_callable_powerindex and test_structure both exercise
`s[ca.vertcat, [...]]`.

Upstream-Status: To upstream [not yet submitted; cannot open issues/PRs against casadi/casadi from this environment]

Signed-off-by: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
---
 swig/python/tools/structure.py | 5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/swig/python/tools/structure.py b/swig/python/tools/structure.py
index 5c768df..8e89792 100644
--- a/swig/python/tools/structure.py
+++ b/swig/python/tools/structure.py
@@ -116,7 +116,10 @@ def applyCallableIndex(p,r):
   # Apply a callable powerIndex entry to the sub-result it indexes
   try:
     return p(r)
-  except NotImplementedError:
+  except (NotImplementedError, TypeError):
+    # vertcat/horzcat/... are SWIG-overloaded free functions, not methods:
+    # a single-list argument that doesn't match any registered overload
+    # raises TypeError from the C++ dispatch, not NotImplementedError.
     if not isinstance(r,list): raise
     return p(*r) # casadi's concatenations (vertcat, ...) are variadic, not list-taking
 
